<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victor Lieberman</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victor Lieberman is an American historian of South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> at the University of Michigan. His Burmese Administrative Cycles (1984) studied the Toungoo state, and his two-volume Strange Parallels (2003–2009) compared state formation in mainland South-East Asia with that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, arguing that they followed similar long-term patterns of integration.</p></div>
